      "writtenOn": "2023-02-06T17:44:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, the problem you have explained is exactly the reason why I came up with this change. I have thought of creating a `java_api_contribution` directly from `java_sdk_library`, but this solution has two drawbacks: The first is that there currently are API domains that contribute to the API surface with a `droidstubs`, not with `java_sdk_library`. Thus, boilerplate `java_api_contribution` modules would have to be written out in bp files for these domains if `java_api_contribution` is created from `java_sdk_library`. Another disadvantage is that any additional droidstubs modules that newly contribute to any API surface would require additional `java_api_contribution` modules definition per surface. However, such problem is resolved when it is created from `droidstubs`, whether a `droidstubs` or `java_sdk_library` is added to API surfaces.",
      "parentUuid": "fc6dc494_d7fd4998",
      "revId": "f9e305a8bc60d16e4fff06c9f65f9bc4f12bb6ef",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
